WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
597 BC.

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:06.730
Babylon takes Jerusalem and
carries off its king and priests.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:12.380
One exile, a priest called Ezekiel, is
called to be a prophet by the river Chebar.

4
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:18.300
He draws a city on a brick, then
lies on his left side for 390 days.

5
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.910
Later his wife dies in one evening.

6
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.610
He is told not to mourn or weep.

7
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.160
Why would a prophet behave like this?

8
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.070
In this mission, you'll follow
his call: a blazing vision,

9
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.020
and a scroll he must eat.

10
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.350
Then you'll weigh up a question
scholars still argue about:

11
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.850
was he ill?

12
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.750
Your mission: find out why a prophet would
lie on his side for 390 days and refuse

13
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.280
to mourn his own wife.
